@startuml
title III-02 - Customer login, refresh-token rotation and logout

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Customer
boundary "Customer Portal" as Web
control "Auth API" as API
database "Auth Database / Redis" as DB

== Login ==

Customer -> Web: Enter email and password
Web -> API: POST /api/auth/login
API -> DB: Find user by email
API -> API: Verify password and account status

alt Invalid credentials or locked account
    API --> Web: 401/423 authentication error
    Web --> Customer: Show login error
else Valid credentials
    API -> API: Create short-lived access JWT
    API -> API: Create refresh token
    API -> API: Hash refresh token
    API -> DB: Store hash, userId, expiresAt, token family,\nstatus ACTIVE, revokeReason NULL
    API --> Web: accessToken\nSet-Cookie refreshToken=...; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite
    Web --> Customer: Open customer portal
    note right of Web
      FE keeps accessToken in memory only.
      Browser manages the refresh cookie.
    end note
end

== Refresh with rotation ==

Customer -> Web: Access token expired
Web -> API: POST /api/auth/refresh\n(refreshToken)
API -> API: Hash presented refresh token
API -> DB: Lock and load the refresh-token record

alt Token missing
    API --> Web: 401 INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN
    Web --> Customer: Redirect to login
else Token expired
    API --> Web: 401 REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRED
    Web --> Customer: Request login again
else Token already rotated or used again
    API -> DB: Revoke entire token family\nreason REUSE_DETECTED
    API -> DB: Record security event
    API --> Web: 401 REFRESH_TOKEN_REUSE_DETECTED
    Web --> Customer: Revoke local session and request login
else Token revoked by logout or admin
    API --> Web: 401 INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN
    Web --> Customer: Request login again
else Active token
    API -> DB: Revoke old token\nreason ROTATED
    API -> API: Create new access JWT
    API -> API: Create and hash replacement refresh token
    API -> DB: Store replacement token with same token family
    API --> Web: New accessToken\nSet-Cookie replacement refreshToken
end

== Logout ==

Customer -> Web: Click logout
Web -> API: POST /api/auth/logout
API -> API: Read refresh token from HttpOnly cookie
API -> API: Hash presented refresh token
API -> DB: Lock and load the current refresh-token record
API -> DB: Revoke current token only\nreason LOGOUT
API --> Web: 204 No Content\nClear refresh cookie
Web --> Customer: Clear local tokens and show login

note over API,DB
  Refresh tokens are stored as hashes and sent only by
  HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite cookies.
  Normal logout revokes the current session only.
  Token-family revocation is reserved for reuse detection.
end note

@enduml
